<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kesho Das of Jhabua</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 1584</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kesho Das was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rathore">Rathore</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> who founded the state of Jhabua in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malwa">Malwa</a> around 1584. According to the state's tradition, he received the title of Raja from the Mughal court after suppressing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhils">Bhil</a> chiefs who had attacked imperial officials, and took Jhabua from its earlier Bhil ruler. His descendants ruled Jhabua as a princely state until it joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> in 1948.</p></div>
